    "body": "## Summary\n\n`ibm-granite/granite-3.0-3b-a800m-instruct` (and likely sibling `granitemoe`/`granitemoehybrid`/`granitemoeshared` models) fails to load with:\n\n```\nValueError: Couldn't instantiate the backend tokenizer from one of:\n(1) a `tokenizers` library serialization file,\n(2) a slow tokenizer instance to convert or\n(3) an equivalent slow tokenizer class to instantiate and convert.\nYou need to have sentencepiece or tiktoken installed to convert a slow tokenizer to a fast one.\n```\n\nRoot cause: this model's `config.json` has `model_type: \"granitemoe\"`, which transformers v5 maps to the generic `TokenizersBackend` in `TOKENIZER_MAPPING_NAMES`. The model's own `tokenizer_config.json` declares `tokenizer_class: \"GPT2Tokenizer\"` (it ships `vocab.json`/`merges.txt`, no `tokenizer.json`). transformers' `AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained` only honors a hub-declared `tokenizer_class` override when the model_type's *registered* class is concrete — since `granitemoe`'s registered class is itself `TokenizersBackend`, the override is skipped and the bare generic backend is instantiated instead, which can't build a tokenizer from `vocab.json`/`merges.txt` alone and raises.\n\nsglang already has `_resolve_tokenizers_backend()` to work around this general class of transformers v5 regression, but it only triggers when `AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained` *succeeds* and returns a `TokenizersBackend` instance. In this case construction raises instead of returning an object, so that fallback path is never reached.\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `_auto_tokenizer_from_pretrained`, when `AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained` raises this specific `ValueError`, fall back to the existing `_load_tokenizer_by_declared_class()` helper, which loads the tokenizer directly via the class `tokenizer_config.json` declares (`GPT2Tokenizer` here), bypassing `AutoTokenizer`'s resolution entirely.\n\n## Test plan\n\nReproduced and validated on real XPU hardware against the exact `lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.21-xpu` release image:\n\n- Before fix: server crashes at tokenizer init with the `ValueError` above, every run.\n- After fix: tokenizer loads via `GPT2Tokenizer`, model loads as `GraniteMoeForCausalLM`, server starts successfully, and a gsm8k eval (5 examples, `lm_eval`) completes with exit code 0 (`exact_match` 0.6, both `flexible-extract` and `strict-match` filters).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38227662757](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38227662757)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38227662352](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38227662352)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38227662770](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38227662770)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
